

3
00:01:13,375 --> 00:01:15,166
<i>Hey, this is Houston.
Do you copy?</i>

4
00:01:15,291 --> 00:01:16,250
Copy Houston.

5
00:01:16,875 --> 00:01:18,374
<i>It's Christy. How's it going?</i>

6
00:01:18,375 --> 00:01:20,125
Hey, Christy,
it's great to hear your voice.

7
00:01:20,375 --> 00:01:22,582
<i>Sam's family wants
to connect with her immediately.</i>

8
00:01:22,583 --> 00:01:23,540
<i>Is she nearby?</i>

9
00:01:23,541 --> 00:01:25,040
She's in the research facility.

10
00:01:25,041 --> 00:01:27,000
- I'll just connect to her.
<i>- Okay, copy!</i>

11
00:01:39,250 --> 00:01:41,208
Sam, you got a call from India.

12
00:02:02,958 --> 00:02:04,791
<i>Your call has been forwarded to a--</i>

13
00:02:05,791 --> 00:02:08,041
- Brother!
- Hello! Welcome, in-laws.

14
00:02:09,375 --> 00:02:10,708
Son-in-law hasn't…

15
00:02:10,833 --> 00:02:12,583
He's on the flight over here.

16
00:02:13,041 --> 00:02:14,665
"Has Adhithi eaten?
Did Adhithi get some sleep?

17
00:02:14,666 --> 00:02:17,166
Did Adhithi like the arrangements?
Did she like the handloom sari?"

18
00:02:17,291 --> 00:02:18,833
In fact, he even inquired about you.

19
00:02:19,083 --> 00:02:20,290
Oh, that's sweet of him.

20
00:02:20,291 --> 00:02:22,750
You don't worry about anything.
I'll handle everything.

21
00:02:22,875 --> 00:02:24,083
He will be here on time.

22
00:02:24,666 --> 00:02:25,708
Why don't you have a drink with me?

23
00:02:25,916 --> 00:02:27,416
It's okay, not now.
You carry on!

24
00:02:27,666 --> 00:02:28,583
Let's go!

25
00:02:30,125 --> 00:02:31,125
<i>That was a close call!</i>

26
00:02:35,000 --> 00:02:36,915
- Come here, damn it!
- Come dance with me, Uncle.

27
00:02:36,916 --> 00:02:38,415
You're dancing unaware of the situation.

28
00:02:38,416 --> 00:02:39,500
And you're inviting me on top of it.

29
00:02:39,666 --> 00:02:40,958
Uncle, he did call, right?

30
00:02:41,750 --> 00:02:44,165
No one has been answering my calls.
How many times should I call them?

31
00:02:44,166 --> 00:02:46,125
- When did you call them?
- Since this morning.

32
00:02:46,250 --> 00:02:47,458
If it's morning here,
it's night out there.

33
00:02:47,708 --> 00:02:49,958
It is only dawn for them now.
Uncle, call them now.

34
00:03:03,833 --> 00:03:04,790
Hello?

35
00:03:04,791 --> 00:03:06,333
Sachin, why aren't you answering my calls?

36
00:03:06,500 --> 00:03:08,415
- Who are you?
- Huh? FBI!

37
00:03:08,416 --> 00:03:10,708
- Haven't you left for the wedding yet?
- Who is getting married?

38
00:03:11,041 --> 00:03:12,540
Bloody sinners! Are you guys drunk?

39
00:03:12,541 --> 00:03:13,458
Uncle!

40
00:03:13,833 --> 00:03:14,832
<i>What are you guys doing?</i>

41
00:03:14,833 --> 00:03:17,249
<i>The wedding is tomorrow. And I don't
see that you guys are serious about it.</i>

42
00:03:17,250 --> 00:03:18,416
<i>Is this how you behave?</i>

43
00:03:19,125 --> 00:03:20,791
How could you guys be so irresponsible?

44
00:03:21,250 --> 00:03:22,457
Everyone here is stressed out.

45
00:03:22,458 --> 00:03:24,041
For God's sake, get here soon.
Please!

46
00:03:24,208 --> 00:03:26,875
Uncle, it's my responsibility
to bring Idhaya to the wedding.

47
00:03:27,000 --> 00:03:28,166
Please hang up.

48
00:03:28,583 --> 00:03:29,875
- Hey, where's Idhaya?
- Idhaya?

49
00:03:30,041 --> 00:03:30,958
Idhaya!

50
00:03:31,083 --> 00:03:32,833
Where the hell is Idhaya?
Idhaya!

51
00:03:32,958 --> 00:03:34,458
- Hey, Idhaya?
- Let me check upstairs.

52
00:03:34,583 --> 00:03:35,583
- Idhaya!
- Idhaya!

53
00:03:36,125 --> 00:03:37,041
Hey!

54
00:03:41,541 --> 00:03:43,958
<i>O Heart of mine</i>

55
00:03:45,666 --> 00:03:47,791
Oh, my God! Look at him.

56
00:03:48,833 --> 00:03:50,666
We're getting late for the flight.
Why aren't you guys ready yet?

57
00:03:52,083 --> 00:03:53,875
Buddy, that's the spirit!

58
00:03:54,791 --> 00:03:56,916
- My best friend is getting married.
- Yay!

59
00:03:57,041 --> 00:03:58,082
What are you guys waiting for?

60
00:03:58,083 --> 00:03:59,707
We only have
two hours for the flight. Scram!

61
00:03:59,708 --> 00:04:01,416
Oh, damn, let's get ready soon.

62
00:04:01,791 --> 00:04:04,625
<i>I've found my way to you</i>

63
00:04:05,500 --> 00:04:07,875
Instead of packing,
why are you throwing it down?

64
00:04:08,166 --> 00:04:10,000
Quickly pack up. We're getting late.

65
00:04:12,250 --> 00:04:13,625
Hey, throw that away.

66
00:04:15,666 --> 00:04:16,582
Here you go!

67
00:04:16,583 --> 00:04:22,208
<i>Your misguided thoughts
Left me drowning in sorrow</i>

68
00:04:22,416 --> 00:04:27,791
<i>Like nectar in every flower,
My heart seeks you every day</i>

69
00:04:39,416 --> 00:04:42,125
<i>Butterflies are fluttering</i>

70
00:04:42,333 --> 00:04:45,083
<i>A game of hide-and-seek is on</i>

71
00:04:45,208 --> 00:04:47,750
<i>Everything looks lush and green</i>

72
00:04:47,916 --> 00:04:50,666
<i>Everything looks lush and green</i>

73
00:04:50,791 --> 00:04:53,500
<i>Butterflies are fluttering</i>

74
00:04:53,708 --> 00:04:56,375
<i>A game of hide-and-seek is on</i>

75
00:04:56,625 --> 00:04:59,250
<i>Everything looks lush and green</i>

76
00:04:59,500 --> 00:05:04,208
<i>Beautiful birds circle in our sight</i>

77
00:05:05,375 --> 00:05:07,791
<i>O Heart of mine</i>

78
00:05:08,333 --> 00:05:11,125
<i>You're one of a kind</i>

79
00:05:11,291 --> 00:05:13,541
<i>O Heart of mine</i>

80
00:05:14,000 --> 00:05:16,625
<i>My throbbing love</i>

81
00:05:26,583 --> 00:05:27,833
Hey, you work out, right?

82
00:05:28,000 --> 00:05:29,499
- Hand it to me.
- Thanks!

83
00:05:29,500 --> 00:05:31,707
- Where's the huge bag?
- Hey, I did not bring it.

84
00:05:31,708 --> 00:05:33,875
- You never asked me to.
- Why do you do this, Priya?

85
00:05:34,041 --> 00:05:36,708
I regret bringing you guys
on business class.

86
00:05:37,125 --> 00:05:38,665
- Oh, God!
- Sir, please sit down.

87
00:05:38,666 --> 00:05:40,333
- Aren't they supposed to serve us juice?
- Sir, please sit down.

88
00:05:40,458 --> 00:05:41,665
Ma'am, please!

89
00:05:41,666 --> 00:05:44,374
- Hey, where are you going?
- I'm going to the loo.

90
00:05:44,375 --> 00:05:45,999
- Do I need permission for it?
- Prabhu, go with him.

91
00:05:46,000 --> 00:05:47,666
- He might jump off the plane.
- Two cannot fit in there.

92
00:05:47,833 --> 00:05:48,833
Fine, I'll adjust

93
00:05:52,416 --> 00:05:53,916
<i>Hey, fool! Fool!</i>

94
00:05:54,250 --> 00:05:55,540
<i>- Did you board the flight or not?</i>
- What?

95
00:05:55,541 --> 00:05:57,583
<i>Bloody dirty pants.
Peg yourself to be a great actor?</i>

96
00:06:00,083 --> 00:06:01,332
- Hello?
<i>- I'll rip you apart.</i>

97
00:06:01,333 --> 00:06:03,500
<i>What's with the hello?
The wedding is tomorrow!</i>

98
00:06:03,666 --> 00:06:05,665
<i>If you don't make it here,
you're as good as dead.</i>

99
00:06:05,666 --> 00:06:07,000
<i>Send me a picture of you
sitting on the flight.</i>

100
00:06:07,208 --> 00:06:08,541
<i>If the wedding gets called off…</i>

101
00:06:17,250 --> 00:06:18,166
Give me the phone.

102
00:06:19,125 --> 00:06:20,041
Phone?

103
00:06:20,708 --> 00:06:22,125
I can't give you my phone, sir.

104
00:06:22,416 --> 00:06:23,708
It contains a lot of personal information.

105
00:06:24,541 --> 00:06:27,125
I don't want your phone.
Give me back my phone.

106
00:06:30,458 --> 00:06:33,208
I'm so sorry.
Same phone and same color.

107
00:06:36,208 --> 00:06:38,125
Is your uncle very short-tempered?

108
00:06:39,791 --> 00:06:42,291
Uncle?
Did my uncle call?

109
00:06:45,125 --> 00:06:46,250
Did you answer the call?

110
00:06:47,041 --> 00:06:48,458
He yelled at me in colorful words.

111
00:06:49,000 --> 00:06:51,666
He said he'd kill you if you didn't
make it to the wedding tomorrow.

112
00:06:52,416 --> 00:06:55,208
Sir, ask him why he's here
when his wedding is tomorrow.

113
00:06:56,791 --> 00:06:57,708
I understand!

114
00:06:58,083 --> 00:07:00,833
You're looking for a scapegoat
to narrate your flashback.

115
00:07:01,375 --> 00:07:02,499
- Am I right?
- No, sir.

116
00:07:02,500 --> 00:07:04,499
I'm not the man for it.
Please find someone else.

117
00:07:04,500 --> 00:07:05,999
- Sir, the others here are foreigners.
- Yes, sir.

118
00:07:06,000 --> 00:07:08,125
Our story is rooted in the native.
Only you'd be the right match.

119
00:07:08,291 --> 00:07:09,541
I'm going to watch TV.

120
00:07:09,750 --> 00:07:12,916
Sir, they offered an $800 coupon
because the TV is not working.

121
00:07:13,041 --> 00:07:14,082
Didn't they offer you?

122
00:07:14,083 --> 00:07:15,708
It's okay. I'll read a book.

123
00:07:17,125 --> 00:07:19,041
Sir, that's a guide manual.

124
00:07:19,541 --> 00:07:21,749
You have no choice
but to listen to our story.

125
00:07:21,750 --> 00:07:22,749
- Yes, sir.
- Sir,

126
00:07:22,750 --> 00:07:24,582
you're tailored to listen
to a flashback.

127
00:07:24,583 --> 00:07:27,333
Wearing shades, a suit,
and sitting next to us.

128
00:07:27,541 --> 00:07:29,915
Sir, it's a love story.
And it's very interesting.

129
00:07:29,916 --> 00:07:32,874
It'll be a time-pass for you.
And a venting session for us.

130
00:07:32,875 --> 00:07:35,541
Sir, even the supporting
actor has two love stories.

131
00:07:35,666 --> 00:07:37,083
- Hear us out, sir.
- Yes, sir.

132
00:07:37,250 --> 00:07:38,166
What's the run-time?

133
00:07:38,416 --> 00:07:40,916
Sir, the first half runs
for 1 hour and 23 minutes.

134
00:07:41,041 --> 00:07:43,040
But the second half is trimmed
to 1 hour and 20 minutes.

135
00:07:43,041 --> 00:07:45,166
Sir, we can complete the movie
within 2 hours and 43 minutes.

136
00:07:45,416 --> 00:07:46,583
Start the film, guys!

137
00:08:09,083 --> 00:08:10,708
<i>We're a mix of 80s and 90s kids.</i>

138
00:08:11,625 --> 00:08:14,416
<i>We're the last chapter
of a slower, gentler world.</i>

139
00:08:14,625 --> 00:08:17,958
<i>Before the world began to race,
even doing nothing felt like happiness.</i>

140
00:08:18,166 --> 00:08:20,166
<i>Back then, happiness was simple.</i>

141
00:08:20,458 --> 00:08:22,500
<i>Lying on the rooftop, gazing at the sky.</i>

142
00:08:22,791 --> 00:08:24,791
<i>Even though it's not much,
our hearts were lighter.</i>

143
00:08:25,083 --> 00:08:27,958
<i>Friends were not profile pictures
or status updates.</i>

144
00:08:28,083 --> 00:08:30,333
<i>But the one who knocks on the door
to call out to play.</i>

145
00:08:30,583 --> 00:08:32,875
<i>No cafe latte or filter coffees.</i>

146
00:08:33,250 --> 00:08:35,416
<i>Five bucks Popsicle,
and two bags of Lays.</i>

147
00:08:35,583 --> 00:08:36,708
<i>That was our world.</i>

148
00:08:37,833 --> 00:08:41,666
<i>Even cycling felt like
we were the King and Queen.</i>

149
00:08:41,916 --> 00:08:44,540
<i>When the street lights come on,
it's time to get back home.</i>

150
00:08:44,541 --> 00:08:45,958
<i>The lights coming on were our deadline.</i>

151
00:08:46,125 --> 00:08:48,625
<i>But the same lights
were our childhood guardian.</i>

152
00:08:49,041 --> 00:08:52,250
<i>When technology advanced,
we embraced and adjusted to it.</i>

153
00:08:52,583 --> 00:08:55,875
<i>Right from the ringing of landlines
to this generation's seen status.</i>

154
00:08:56,000 --> 00:08:58,000
<i>But our world wasn't a virtual one.</i>

155
00:08:58,333 --> 00:09:00,000
<i>The scent of rain and sand,</i>

156
00:09:00,333 --> 00:09:02,625
<i>open playgrounds,
our mother's voice calling out to us…</i>

157
00:09:02,958 --> 00:09:04,166
<i>Those were our ring-tones.</i>

158
00:09:04,583 --> 00:09:07,000
<i>Back then, life wasn't loud but light.</i>

159
00:09:09,916 --> 00:09:11,791
<i>We're bearing both versions of the world.</i>

160
00:09:12,083 --> 00:09:15,708
<i>From the time when VHS tapes
gave us irreplaceable memories.</i>

161
00:09:16,458 --> 00:09:17,750
<i>We'll never get those days back.</i>

162
00:09:17,958 --> 00:09:19,875
<i>However, it hasn't left us.</i>

163
00:09:20,125 --> 00:09:21,541
<i>They're still alive in us.</i>

164
00:09:21,750 --> 00:09:24,000
<i>It's alive in our smile, memories…</i>

165
00:09:24,250 --> 00:09:27,500
<i>That indescribable feeling
when an old song slows your heartbeat.</i>

166
00:09:33,958 --> 00:09:35,750
<i>We're the last simple generation.</i>

167
00:09:35,875 --> 00:09:38,500
<i>But we're the first magic generation.</i>

168
00:09:48,958 --> 00:09:51,666
Hey, Idhaya, hot water is ready.
Quickly take a shower.

169
00:09:51,833 --> 00:09:54,416
Uncle, let me watch some more TV
and then take a shower.

170
00:09:54,875 --> 00:09:56,957
How long will you wear these dirty pants
without taking a shower?

171
00:09:56,958 --> 00:09:59,375
- Uncle, let me watch TV for some time.
- Stop watching TV up close.

172
00:09:59,916 --> 00:10:01,125
<i>I don't have parents.</i>

173
00:10:01,875 --> 00:10:03,208
<i>But I have my uncle.</i>

174
00:10:03,833 --> 00:10:05,041
<i>He's everything for me.</i>

175
00:10:07,291 --> 00:10:08,250
Why are you guys late?

176
00:10:08,416 --> 00:10:09,958
- I woke up late, dude.
- Run! Run!

177
00:10:10,208 --> 00:10:11,999
- Me too.
- Once again, they're late to school.

178
00:10:12,000 --> 00:10:12,916
- Come.
- Sir!

179
00:10:13,208 --> 00:10:15,750
The last bell has rung,
and everyone is rushing in.

180
00:10:15,916 --> 00:10:18,166
But you guys are happily taking your time.

181
00:10:20,083 --> 00:10:22,625
<i>In our school lives,
we all have one favorite teacher.</i>

182
00:10:22,916 --> 00:10:25,166
<i>Affectionate, caring, and close to us.</i>

183
00:10:25,416 --> 00:10:26,833
<i>Yes, beautiful, too.</i>

184
00:10:27,333 --> 00:10:29,083
<i>And that's what
Geetha teacher meant to me.</i>

185
00:10:29,416 --> 00:10:30,625
<i>My English teacher.</i>

186
00:10:51,791 --> 00:10:54,625
Prabhu, my tooth came off.

187
00:10:55,416 --> 00:10:58,291
Then rush and bury it
without anyone knowing.

188
00:10:58,416 --> 00:10:59,333
Why?

189
00:10:59,708 --> 00:11:01,541
Only then will a new tooth grow.

190
00:11:01,958 --> 00:11:03,166
Are you guys telling the truth?

191
00:11:03,708 --> 00:11:05,457
Why? Aren't you aware of it?

192
00:11:05,458 --> 00:11:06,375
I don't know.

193
00:11:09,916 --> 00:11:13,416
Hey, don't eat the seeds.
A tree will grow inside your stomach.

194
00:11:15,250 --> 00:11:16,375
Are you guys telling the truth?

195
00:11:16,666 --> 00:11:20,041
- Hey, he's got twin swirls on his head.
- Yes!

196
00:11:20,625 --> 00:11:22,583
That means he'll marry two wives.

197
00:11:23,291 --> 00:11:24,666
Are you guys telling the truth?

198
00:11:27,125 --> 00:11:28,415
Good morning, students!

199
00:11:28,416 --> 00:11:30,916
Good morning, teacher!

200
00:11:32,500 --> 00:11:36,458
In this year's annual day event,
who is willing to participate?

201
00:11:36,958 --> 00:11:39,375
Hey, don't raise your hands.

202
00:11:39,583 --> 00:11:41,416
It'll be humiliating on the stage.

203
00:11:44,458 --> 00:11:45,458
Idhaya!

204
00:11:46,708 --> 00:11:48,958
- Aren't you interested?
- I'm interested, Teacher.

205
00:11:51,500 --> 00:11:52,416
Good!

206
00:11:53,750 --> 00:11:55,666
Even Prabhu and Dravid are interested.

207
00:12:00,250 --> 00:12:01,166
Very good!

208
00:12:04,458 --> 00:12:06,958
- Check if it's clear now.
- Hey, is the transmission clear?

209
00:12:07,875 --> 00:12:08,791
No!

210
00:12:09,041 --> 00:12:10,666
It's not clear yet, Uncle!

211
00:12:11,958 --> 00:12:12,875
Wait a minute!

212
00:12:15,916 --> 00:12:16,916
It must be clear now.

213
00:12:18,625 --> 00:12:19,541
Now?

214
00:12:29,041 --> 00:12:30,916
What are they doing, guys?

215
00:12:31,291 --> 00:12:34,083
They're planning to have a baby.

216
00:12:34,583 --> 00:12:36,208
How do you know about this?

217
00:12:36,458 --> 00:12:39,291
Didn't you see them kiss?

218
00:12:39,583 --> 00:12:40,500
Hey, Idhaya!

219
00:12:40,875 --> 00:12:42,250
So what if they kissed?

220
00:12:42,458 --> 00:12:45,249
Don't you know
that kissing can lead to pregnancy?

221
00:12:45,250 --> 00:12:46,625
Are you guys telling the truth?

222
00:12:46,750 --> 00:12:48,500
Aren't you aware of it?

223
00:12:48,708 --> 00:12:50,083
No, I know about it.

224
00:12:50,625 --> 00:12:52,583
Still, let's clarify with brother Sachin.

225
00:12:52,750 --> 00:12:55,500
You're right.
Brother will give us clarity.

226
00:12:56,375 --> 00:12:57,541
That's right, guys!

227
00:12:57,750 --> 00:13:00,333
Kissing will lead to pregnancy.
Don't you guys know?

228
00:13:00,541 --> 00:13:03,290
I'm ashamed to call you guys my juniors.

229
00:13:03,291 --> 00:13:04,207
Damn!

230
00:13:04,208 --> 00:13:05,750
How would we know, brother?

231
00:13:06,750 --> 00:13:08,125
That's why we came to you.

232
00:13:08,250 --> 00:13:10,500
I have to teach you guys everything.

233
00:13:10,625 --> 00:13:12,333
Fine, there's nothing I can do about it.

234
00:13:12,541 --> 00:13:13,875
Because you're like
younger brothers to me.

235
00:13:14,708 --> 00:13:17,665
Now we're going to witness
the fancy dress competition

236
00:13:17,666 --> 00:13:21,166
of our 1998 Annual Day celebration.

237
00:13:21,458 --> 00:13:23,916
First of all,
we're welcoming The Hanuman.

238
00:13:30,958 --> 00:13:33,250
Good evening, I'm Abraham Lincoln.

239
00:13:33,375 --> 00:13:36,708
I'm the 16th President
of the United States of America.

240
00:13:37,000 --> 00:13:37,916
Thank you.

241
00:13:38,708 --> 00:13:41,374
Hello, everyone!
I'm Netaji Subash Chandra Bose.

242
00:13:41,375 --> 00:13:42,874
A freedom fighter of India.

243
00:13:42,875 --> 00:13:43,791
Jai Hind!

244
00:13:48,791 --> 00:13:51,458
I am… Neil Armstrong…

245
00:13:53,583 --> 00:13:54,541
I am…

246
00:13:56,541 --> 00:13:57,458
I am…

247
00:13:59,791 --> 00:14:00,708
Neil…

248
00:14:03,291 --> 00:14:04,541
Armstrong…

249
00:14:06,250 --> 00:14:07,166
Idhaya!

250
00:14:08,208 --> 00:14:09,125
Idhaya!

251
00:14:12,458 --> 00:14:13,458
What happened?

252
00:14:15,166 --> 00:14:16,541
I'm right here beside you.

253
00:14:18,375 --> 00:14:19,583
Speak confidently.

254
00:14:23,291 --> 00:14:25,041
That's a small step for a man.

255
00:14:25,500 --> 00:14:27,625
One giant leap for mankind.

256
00:14:41,083 --> 00:14:43,583
You spoke brilliantly, Idhaya.
It was amazing.

257
00:14:45,625 --> 00:14:46,583
Thank you, Teacher.

258
00:15:00,916 --> 00:15:03,791
<i>Don't you know
that kissing can lead to pregnancy?</i>

259
00:15:20,541 --> 00:15:21,500
Uncle!

260
00:15:22,875 --> 00:15:25,624
How are babies born?

261
00:15:25,625 --> 00:15:26,583
Hey, dirty pants!

262
00:15:26,833 --> 00:15:28,958
Holy shit! What are you saying?

263
00:15:29,416 --> 00:15:31,458
Idhaya, it's a very big mistake.

264
00:15:32,916 --> 00:15:34,290
Shall we start from one?

265
00:15:34,291 --> 00:15:35,958
<i>- So, I was scared since then…</i>
- One.

266
00:15:36,750 --> 00:15:39,457
<i>…thinking if Geetha teacher's stomach
will start growing.</i>

267
00:15:39,458 --> 00:15:40,458
Nothing, Teacher.

268
00:15:47,541 --> 00:15:48,791
You're behind three months.

269
00:15:51,083 --> 00:15:53,041
- Hey, hold the baby for me.
- I won't!

270
00:15:53,166 --> 00:15:54,083
Hey, hold the baby!

271
00:15:54,458 --> 00:15:55,957
Hey, Idhaya!
Why is he running scared?

272
00:15:55,958 --> 00:15:56,875
Hey, it's raining!

273
00:16:09,791 --> 00:16:11,541
Good morning! Good morning!

274
00:16:11,750 --> 00:16:13,333
Good morning, Teacher!

275
00:16:13,458 --> 00:16:15,500
How were your summer holidays?

276
00:16:16,291 --> 00:16:18,583
You guys are no longer in your 4th grade

277
00:16:18,791 --> 00:16:20,541
but you have graduated to the 5th grade.

278
00:16:21,583 --> 00:16:24,374
<i>I was scared after looking
at Geetha teacher's stomach.</i>

279
00:16:24,375 --> 00:16:28,541
This year we have a new student
in our class.

280
00:16:30,041 --> 00:16:33,291
<i>In that moment, I decided that
Geetha teacher's child is my child.</i>

281
00:16:33,500 --> 00:16:34,791
<i>It's our child.</i>

282
00:16:35,625 --> 00:16:38,790
<i>I decided to take care
of her and the child.</i>

283
00:16:38,791 --> 00:16:39,749
May I help you?

284
00:16:39,750 --> 00:16:41,458
- Oh, do you want to help me?
- Yes!

285
00:16:42,083 --> 00:16:43,000
Okay.

286
00:17:34,000 --> 00:17:35,000
Hey, let's go inside.

287
00:17:35,833 --> 00:17:37,166
Teacher, what happened to you?

288
00:17:37,666 --> 00:17:39,665
- What happened?
- Please call for an auto.

289
00:17:39,666 --> 00:17:40,666
Idhaya, hurry up!

290
00:17:47,750 --> 00:17:49,958
Auto! Auto!

291
00:17:51,541 --> 00:17:52,541
Please help me.

292
00:17:53,833 --> 00:17:54,750
What happened, son?

293
00:17:54,916 --> 00:17:56,833
She's in labor.
We have to go to the hospital.

294
00:17:56,958 --> 00:17:58,458
Is it your mother?

295
00:17:59,583 --> 00:18:01,040
- No!
- Then who?

296
00:18:01,041 --> 00:18:02,208
- Idhaya!
- Teacher!

297
00:18:04,500 --> 00:18:05,416
I'm coming, ma'am.

298
00:18:06,750 --> 00:18:07,750
You'll be fine, Teacher!

299
00:18:07,916 --> 00:18:08,916
Be careful…

300
00:18:11,125 --> 00:18:13,165
Nurse!
Bring a gurney, it's an emergency.

301
00:18:13,166 --> 00:18:14,791
- Teacher, please don't fear.
- Hold the umbrella.

302
00:18:14,916 --> 00:18:16,125
Come on, hurry up!

303
00:18:30,541 --> 00:18:31,832
Brother, where can I find a phone?

304
00:18:31,833 --> 00:18:32,958
Go straight and take the last right.

305
00:19:01,791 --> 00:19:04,708
Kids, I've informed your teacher's family.

306
00:19:05,000 --> 00:19:06,166
They'll be here soon.

307
00:19:06,416 --> 00:19:08,541
Your folks must be looking for you guys.
Let's go.

308
00:19:09,333 --> 00:19:12,458
I appreciate it.
You guys did so much for your teacher.

309
00:19:12,750 --> 00:19:14,041
It's not for our teacher.

310
00:19:16,166 --> 00:19:17,541
But for his wife.

311
00:19:20,333 --> 00:19:22,500
Almost everyone in this world
has had a crush on a teacher.

312
00:19:23,250 --> 00:19:25,791
That's the inception of unrequited love.

313
00:19:29,166 --> 00:19:30,500
Fine, let's go home.

314
00:19:37,958 --> 00:19:41,333
Hey, why is he getting emotional
like 'Idhayam' Murali?

315
00:19:42,291 --> 00:19:43,333
Hey!

316
00:19:45,541 --> 00:19:48,250
Let's go. There'll be more things
in life to get emotional about.

317
00:19:49,291 --> 00:19:50,208
Get in!

318
00:19:52,375 --> 00:19:54,416
<i>After that,
I never saw Geetha teacher.</i>

319
00:19:54,916 --> 00:19:57,166
<i>I was told that she quit her job
and moved to another city.</i>

320
00:19:57,833 --> 00:19:59,958
<i>That was the last day
I saw Geetha teacher.</i>

321
00:20:02,875 --> 00:20:06,125
Where was her husband
while you were signing the form?

322
00:20:06,291 --> 00:20:08,541
Sir, he was a sincere shepherd.

323
00:20:08,750 --> 00:20:10,750
He was abroad herding white sheep.

324
00:20:10,875 --> 00:20:13,000
He left a pregnant woman alone
on the verge of delivery.

325
00:20:13,208 --> 00:20:14,750
He must be a classic jerk.

326
00:20:15,666 --> 00:20:17,083
Indeed, he's a jerk.

327
00:20:17,208 --> 00:20:20,500
Sir, after that breakup, his tender
heart was torn into many pieces.

328
00:20:20,916 --> 00:20:21,875
I understood!

329
00:20:22,250 --> 00:20:24,207
Leave out love stories
that didn't work out.

330
00:20:24,208 --> 00:20:25,875
Just narrate the ones that worked out.

331
00:20:26,250 --> 00:20:29,250
<i>Today, we'll be discussing corrosion.</i>

332
00:20:29,458 --> 00:20:32,375
You must be familiar
with the rusting of iron.

333
00:20:32,625 --> 00:20:34,957
Green patches on a copper vessel.

334
00:20:34,958 --> 00:20:36,541
And brass vessels.

335
00:20:41,166 --> 00:20:42,083
Hey!

336
00:20:42,500 --> 00:20:44,833
- The bell will ring, right?
- Yes, it will ring.

337
00:20:45,166 --> 00:20:46,125
What if it's broken?

338
00:20:46,458 --> 00:20:47,500
I will ring it myself.

339
00:20:48,500 --> 00:20:51,041
…most commonly with oxygen.

340
00:20:52,166 --> 00:20:53,166
Sit down, please.

341
00:20:53,375 --> 00:20:55,375
Let me finish my explanation.

342
00:20:55,541 --> 00:20:57,500
Then I can allow you to go.

343
00:20:57,833 --> 00:21:00,165
Corrosion is a natural process.

344
00:21:00,166 --> 00:21:01,791
Hey, will he let us go or not?

345
00:21:01,958 --> 00:21:04,666
Hey, he'll let us go.
Be patient for five minutes.

346
00:21:04,875 --> 00:21:07,000
…stable chemical state.

347
00:21:08,166 --> 00:21:09,750
Please stand for the prayer.

348
00:21:09,875 --> 00:21:11,750
- Our Father…
- Our Father…

349
00:21:11,875 --> 00:21:14,290
-…who art in heaven…
-…who art in heaven…

350
00:21:14,291 --> 00:21:16,915
-…lead us not into temptation…
-…lead us not into temptation…

351
00:21:16,916 --> 00:21:19,332
-…but deliver us from evil.
-…but deliver us from evil.

352
00:21:19,333 --> 00:21:20,500
- Amen!
- Amen!

353
00:21:20,625 --> 00:21:22,916
Okay, boys! See you all tomorrow.

354
00:21:23,500 --> 00:21:24,875
Where is he rushing off to?

355
00:21:36,083 --> 00:21:37,083
Who is he?

356
00:21:37,416 --> 00:21:38,875
Where does he go with him every evening?

357
00:21:39,208 --> 00:21:40,708
He comes to pick him up daily.

358
00:21:46,916 --> 00:21:48,666
Dude, he's having something.

359
00:21:51,583 --> 00:21:53,916
- Let's inquire what's happening.
- Hey, don't go.

360
00:21:54,208 --> 00:21:55,708
He looks dangerous.

361
00:21:56,583 --> 00:21:57,500
Don't be scared!

362
00:21:57,666 --> 00:21:58,874
Hey, I'm running away.

363
00:21:58,875 --> 00:22:00,707
Hey, he's looking at us.
Let's go away.

364
00:22:00,708 --> 00:22:02,541
Hey, turn around casually.
Let's go.

365
00:22:02,708 --> 00:22:03,707
Why are you scared of him?

366
00:22:03,708 --> 00:22:05,458
- We're getting late.
- Hey, I was praying for us.

367
00:22:05,666 --> 00:22:06,791
Ride faster.

368
00:22:13,333 --> 00:22:14,416
- Idhaya!
- Coming!

369
00:22:14,583 --> 00:22:15,499
Bye, Uncle.

370
00:22:15,500 --> 00:22:17,458
Don't go on an empty stomach.
At least have some tea.

371
00:22:18,583 --> 00:22:19,583
Oh, no!

372
00:22:20,500 --> 00:22:22,000
- I'm getting late, Uncle.
- Stop acting. Come here.

373
00:22:26,666 --> 00:22:28,375
Two things I love the most in this world.

374
00:22:28,625 --> 00:22:30,458
- One is your tea.
- What's the second one?

375
00:22:31,333 --> 00:22:33,208
- Dude, come on!
- Oh, no!

376
00:22:33,833 --> 00:22:34,750
I won't reveal it.

377
00:22:35,625 --> 00:22:37,332
- Love you. Bye, Uncle.
- Hey! Hey! Hey!

378
00:22:37,333 --> 00:22:38,916
Hey, reveal it.

379
00:22:40,375 --> 00:22:41,832
In the evening, we have practice.
Don't forget.

380
00:22:41,833 --> 00:22:42,790
We have a match coming up.

381
00:22:42,791 --> 00:22:44,040
- Hey, I have to go.
- Bye!

382
00:22:44,041 --> 00:22:45,291
Dravid, bye! Prabhu, bye!

383
00:22:46,208 --> 00:22:47,333
{\an8}Bye, guys! Bye, bye, bye!

384
00:23:00,041 --> 00:23:00,958
Idhaya.

385
00:23:01,958 --> 00:23:04,291
- Hi, guys! When did you come?
- Just now.

386
00:23:05,166 --> 00:23:06,166
Meet my friend, Juju.

387
00:23:07,000 --> 00:23:07,916
Hi.

388
00:23:08,875 --> 00:23:09,791
Hey, Idhaya.

389
00:23:10,083 --> 00:23:12,707
Let's go. Boys are waiting
at the pitch to practice cricket.

390
00:23:12,708 --> 00:23:16,249
Hey, Juju has come here to meet me.

391
00:23:16,250 --> 00:23:17,500
He'll feel bad.

392
00:23:17,833 --> 00:23:19,791
Yes, bro! Don't take him away.
I'll be bored.

393
00:23:21,541 --> 00:23:23,916
- Hey, Smack--
- Hey, let's go. Let's go.

394
00:23:26,083 --> 00:23:27,249
Switched off or not, I won.

395
00:23:27,250 --> 00:23:28,250
Why did you switch it off?

396
00:23:28,458 --> 00:23:30,207
You are always hanging out with him.

397
00:23:30,208 --> 00:23:31,791
You go away with him in the evening.

398
00:23:31,958 --> 00:23:33,415
Lately, you've been avoiding us.

399
00:23:33,416 --> 00:23:34,665
Why are you friends with a rowdy?

400
00:23:34,666 --> 00:23:36,041
Juju is my friend.

401
00:23:36,291 --> 00:23:38,041
Where do you both go every evening?

402
00:23:41,250 --> 00:23:42,958
Go, Juju, ride faster!

403
00:23:43,750 --> 00:23:45,666
Hey, we're late. Hurry up!

404
00:23:46,125 --> 00:23:47,375
Dude, why are you always late?

405
00:23:47,583 --> 00:23:48,957
That guy is grumpy. He'll yell at us.

406
00:23:48,958 --> 00:23:50,458
Live it up! We're the boys!

407
00:23:52,041 --> 00:23:53,666
Here, hold this! Let's go!

408
00:23:55,458 --> 00:23:57,125
- I'll go first!
- No, I'll go first!

409
00:24:24,250 --> 00:24:25,333
That's my shot!

410
00:24:25,458 --> 00:24:26,374
Yes!

411
00:24:26,375 --> 00:24:27,666
Why is your girl standing idle?

412
00:24:27,916 --> 00:24:30,750
- Hey, Coach!
- Hey, why are you guys late?

413
00:24:32,125 --> 00:24:33,415
Sir, tire puncture.

414
00:24:33,416 --> 00:24:34,875
- Tire puncture, you say.
- Yes, sir.

415
00:24:35,083 --> 00:24:37,333
- Sir, were you plucking grass?
- No, sir.

416
00:24:37,500 --> 00:24:39,083
- That shot was really nice.
- Really?

417
00:24:40,208 --> 00:24:42,625
Son, eyes over here.

418
00:24:43,833 --> 00:24:44,999
I was observing the balls, sir.

419
00:24:45,000 --> 00:24:46,833
Wow! Observing balls?

420
00:24:47,125 --> 00:24:48,874
- Why not bat?
- Bat…

421
00:24:48,875 --> 00:24:49,958
- Bat, sir.
- Oh, you have it already.

422
00:24:50,208 --> 00:24:52,291
- No more coming late. Okay?
- Okay, sir.

423
00:24:53,583 --> 00:24:55,291
- Today's game went well.
- Yes!

424
00:24:55,833 --> 00:24:56,750
Thank you, Coach.

425
00:24:59,041 --> 00:25:00,250
- Bye-bye.
- Bye, Coach.

426
00:25:01,625 --> 00:25:02,541
Damn!

427
00:25:02,750 --> 00:25:03,666
The court is this way.

428
00:25:07,041 --> 00:25:08,707
Everyone is holding a book,
but you don't have one.

429
00:25:08,708 --> 00:25:10,207
We're not here to study.
I'll take one from him.

430
00:25:10,208 --> 00:25:11,041
Oh, no, my book!

431
00:25:13,500 --> 00:25:15,041
I'm happy I got to see my girl.

432
00:25:24,666 --> 00:25:26,166
I'm going to talk to her today.

433
00:25:26,291 --> 00:25:27,208
Thirty one.

434
00:25:29,250 --> 00:25:30,207
What is 31?

435
00:25:30,208 --> 00:25:32,082
You have told me 31 times
that you will speak to her.

436
00:25:32,083 --> 00:25:33,000
But you haven't till now.

437
00:25:33,250 --> 00:25:35,457
I feel confident today
that I'll speak to her.

438
00:25:35,458 --> 00:25:37,166
At least I will borrow
the focus guide from her.

439
00:25:39,666 --> 00:25:41,583
<i>Hey, come on, come here…</i>

440
00:25:41,750 --> 00:25:42,666
Juju!

441
00:25:43,208 --> 00:25:45,583
<i>Are you the gift fate gave me?</i>

442
00:25:48,583 --> 00:25:50,125
- It's over!
- 32.

443
00:25:53,083 --> 00:25:54,082
Come on! We'll do it tomorrow.

444
00:25:54,083 --> 00:25:55,790
Shut up! You're doing it on purpose.

445
00:25:55,791 --> 00:25:57,375
<i>Hey, come on, come here</i>

446
00:25:58,458 --> 00:26:00,625
<i>Are you the gift fate gave me?</i>

447
00:26:02,625 --> 00:26:05,541
Does anyone have a doubt about
Newton's Law, which we learned yesterday?

448
00:26:05,666 --> 00:26:06,583
Sir!

449
00:26:07,541 --> 00:26:10,082
Would you please also teach us
Newton's second law of motion?

450
00:26:10,083 --> 00:26:11,874
Good, this is what a good student is.

451
00:26:11,875 --> 00:26:13,166
No one else is asking a question.

452
00:26:13,291 --> 00:26:15,415
Imagine when we're cycling…

453
00:26:15,416 --> 00:26:17,500
I have an idea
to make our girls turn around.

454
00:26:17,750 --> 00:26:19,083
- What idea?
- Watch me.

455
00:26:19,750 --> 00:26:22,082
- Sir!
- Look, everyone is turning around.

456
00:26:22,083 --> 00:26:24,041
- I don't know anything.
- I don't know, either!

457
00:26:26,500 --> 00:26:28,250
- What is it?
- Sir, I have a doubt.

458
00:26:28,625 --> 00:26:29,583
What is your doubt?

459
00:26:29,833 --> 00:26:31,583
- Gautham asked you a doubt.
- Yes.

460
00:26:31,750 --> 00:26:33,625
If you explain it again,
it'll be helpful.

461
00:26:34,166 --> 00:26:36,208
If you could repeat Gautham's question…

462
00:26:36,541 --> 00:26:37,750
I will give you the answer.

463
00:26:39,041 --> 00:26:40,750
My doubt is cleared, sir.
It's cleared, sir.

464
00:26:40,875 --> 00:26:43,374
- It's clear. Absolutely cleared.
- Oh, clear?

465
00:26:43,375 --> 00:26:44,624
He was asking for the sake of it.

466
00:26:44,625 --> 00:26:45,999
- So, you understood?
- Yes, sir.

467
00:26:46,000 --> 00:26:47,666
Fine, now share with us.

468
00:26:48,416 --> 00:26:50,624
I understood, sir. I understood!

469
00:26:50,625 --> 00:26:52,207
- Okay.
- "Okay" is his answer.

470
00:26:52,208 --> 00:26:53,915
- Okay, sir.
- Sit down.

471
00:26:53,916 --> 00:26:55,249
Everyone turned around.

472
00:26:55,250 --> 00:26:57,083
Juju, you're amazing.

473
00:26:57,250 --> 00:26:58,375
It's a fantastic idea.

474
00:27:13,041 --> 00:27:15,208
Wondering why the coach is drinking cola?

475
00:27:15,375 --> 00:27:17,250
How many of you like to drink cola?

476
00:27:17,416 --> 00:27:18,333
Sir, me! Me!

477
00:27:18,541 --> 00:27:19,458
So, all of you!

478
00:27:19,625 --> 00:27:20,625
Good! Good! Good! Good!

479
00:27:21,125 --> 00:27:23,250
So, this can is your target.

480
00:27:25,375 --> 00:27:29,165
Now, you should serve to hit the target.

481
00:27:29,166 --> 00:27:32,333
Whoever fails to serve properly
will be served by me.

482
00:27:32,458 --> 00:27:33,375
Okay?

483
00:27:33,500 --> 00:27:36,040
Sir, how's that possible? The target
is quite far! Shall I bring it closer?

484
00:27:36,041 --> 00:27:37,791
What were you doing
all these days at practice?

485
00:27:38,125 --> 00:27:39,041
Now, serve!

486
00:27:39,208 --> 00:27:40,583
Aim at the bloody can.

487
00:27:45,708 --> 00:27:47,583
Why are you meddling with the balls?

488
00:27:47,958 --> 00:27:48,875
Come here!

489
00:27:51,833 --> 00:27:53,416
Hey, hey, hey, hey!

490
00:27:54,083 --> 00:27:58,000
Go to the women's court
and pick up balls.

491
00:28:01,083 --> 00:28:02,208
Okay, sir. Thank you.

492
00:28:03,458 --> 00:28:06,875
Why is he so happy about it?
Next, you!

493
00:28:09,541 --> 00:28:10,458
Juju!

494
00:28:11,833 --> 00:28:12,749
Now, you serve!

495
00:28:12,750 --> 00:28:14,332
If I miss,
will I be given the same punishment?

496
00:28:14,333 --> 00:28:15,916
You? Missing the target?

497
