Juju, please wrap this gift.

737
00:40:50,916 --> 00:40:52,000
- Gift wrap?
- Yeah.

738
00:40:52,208 --> 00:40:53,790
- Is this why you called me?
- Yes.

739
00:40:53,791 --> 00:40:56,083
- Here I come.
- Wrap these separately.

740
00:40:56,375 --> 00:40:58,083
Why are you separating the love pigeons?

741
00:40:58,791 --> 00:41:01,165
She's smiling.
Okay, I'll wrap them.

742
00:41:01,166 --> 00:41:02,125
Can I get sellotape?

743
00:41:02,666 --> 00:41:04,582
- Sellotape?
- Wait, let me check.

744
00:41:04,583 --> 00:41:05,915
I'll check.

745
00:41:05,916 --> 00:41:06,958
Check over there.

746
00:41:16,666 --> 00:41:17,583
Come on!

747
00:41:18,125 --> 00:41:19,041
Over there.

748
00:41:19,500 --> 00:41:20,500
I found it.

749
00:41:44,083 --> 00:41:46,250
Hey, what are you looking at?

750
00:41:46,541 --> 00:41:47,541
Are they twins?

751
00:41:47,833 --> 00:41:49,375
Yeah, they're twins!

752
00:41:54,083 --> 00:41:55,957
- Who was at the coaching class?
- Samantha.

753
00:41:55,958 --> 00:41:57,874
- Who was at the tennis class?
- Samyuktha.

754
00:41:57,875 --> 00:41:59,250
- Twins?
- Yeah!

755
00:41:59,416 --> 00:42:00,583
You didn't know?

756
00:42:00,708 --> 00:42:01,791
You're kidding, right?

757
00:42:02,041 --> 00:42:03,000
Hey, please shut up.

758
00:42:03,125 --> 00:42:04,666
- Juju?
- Idhaya, don't give her the gift.

759
00:42:04,791 --> 00:42:06,416
Give the CD to the girl
who came to the coaching class.

760
00:42:10,916 --> 00:42:12,875
How was the class today?

761
00:42:13,541 --> 00:42:15,208
Because of you,
I had to attend the coaching class.

762
00:42:15,583 --> 00:42:17,415
I did not study for the test.

763
00:42:17,416 --> 00:42:18,333
Hey, Dad is here.

764
00:42:19,875 --> 00:42:20,790
Shall we leave?

765
00:42:20,791 --> 00:42:23,083
<i>Happy birthday to you…</i>

766
00:42:26,958 --> 00:42:30,125
Hey, I told you many times
not to use my clothes.

767
00:42:30,416 --> 00:42:32,458
Likewise, don't touch my makeup.

768
00:42:32,583 --> 00:42:33,500
Get lost!

769
00:42:38,458 --> 00:42:42,624
This is the problem Juju hid behind
a rewritten question.

770
00:42:42,625 --> 00:42:43,541
Is it?

771
00:42:58,208 --> 00:43:01,500
Dude, you fell in love with the girl
who attended the coaching class.

772
00:43:01,958 --> 00:43:03,708
Moreover, it was she who noticed you.

773
00:43:04,041 --> 00:43:05,665
The girl who came to tennis class
ignored you.

774
00:43:05,666 --> 00:43:07,416
You propose to the girl
who came to the coaching class.

775
00:43:07,541 --> 00:43:08,832
That's the right thing to do.

776
00:43:08,833 --> 00:43:10,583
- He's right.
- Yes, dude, that'll be right to do.

777
00:43:12,458 --> 00:43:15,250
As you're twins
you guys must be having fun.

778
00:43:15,375 --> 00:43:18,375
We used to switch places
and attend coaching and tennis classes.

779
00:43:18,791 --> 00:43:21,125
How is it possible?
They could recognize you easily.

780
00:43:21,416 --> 00:43:22,958
You guys don't believe me, right?

781
00:43:23,125 --> 00:43:24,082
Wait!

782
00:43:24,083 --> 00:43:26,625
Juju, Idhaya, please come over here.

783
00:43:26,916 --> 00:43:28,833
Why is she calling me?
What's with her?

784
00:43:29,041 --> 00:43:30,208
Who's the coaching class Sam?

785
00:43:30,375 --> 00:43:31,791
Identify who.

786
00:43:32,125 --> 00:43:33,499
Only today did we know they're twins.

787
00:43:33,500 --> 00:43:34,583
How do we identify her?

788
00:43:34,916 --> 00:43:35,833
Go ahead, give it a shot.

789
00:43:57,166 --> 00:44:00,375
Hey, Idhaya, I was the one who invited you
at the coaching class.

790
00:44:01,666 --> 00:44:04,833
See, I told you.
He won't be able to recognize.

791
00:44:07,583 --> 00:44:09,000
You girls are repeatedly hurting him.

792
00:44:28,166 --> 00:44:29,874
Are you single? Or twins?

793
00:44:29,875 --> 00:44:30,791
I'm not a twin.

794
00:44:31,083 --> 00:44:33,041
- But I'm committed.
- Hi, baby.

795
00:44:33,708 --> 00:44:34,625
Brother!

796
00:44:34,916 --> 00:44:36,582
- You were saying something.
- It's okay.

797
00:44:36,583 --> 00:44:38,249
Brother, I heard it.

798
00:44:38,250 --> 00:44:39,915
- Single and all…
- Let it go.

799
00:44:39,916 --> 00:44:41,457
Bro, it's okay to say it.

800
00:44:41,458 --> 00:44:43,832
Aren't you guys in a relationship?
Why are you nagging me?

801
00:44:43,833 --> 00:44:45,333
Annoying people
hurting us again and again.

802
00:45:05,625 --> 00:45:07,540
Idhaya! Idhaya!

803
00:45:07,541 --> 00:45:09,500
Hey, Idhaya, what happened?

804
00:45:10,625 --> 00:45:11,625
Open the door.

805
00:45:16,750 --> 00:45:18,666
Hey, Idhaya, say something.

806
00:45:21,958 --> 00:45:23,583
Hey, what happened?

807
00:45:32,791 --> 00:45:34,791
What happened to the guys
from those two benches?

808
00:45:35,250 --> 00:45:36,166
They are absent, sir.

809
00:45:40,666 --> 00:45:42,833
I don't know what to do after 5 p.m.

810
00:45:53,750 --> 00:45:56,583
<i>After that, I stopped going
to coaching and tennis to see her.</i>

811
00:45:56,708 --> 00:45:59,333
<i>Because I thought it was one,
but I fell for two girls.</i>

812
00:45:59,958 --> 00:46:02,041
<i>I'm clueless with whom I fell in love.</i>

813
00:46:02,583 --> 00:46:04,166
<i>I fell in love with only one girl.</i>

814
00:46:04,541 --> 00:46:05,541
<i>But I lost…</i>

815
00:46:09,458 --> 00:46:11,041
That's an interesting plot twist.

816
00:46:11,625 --> 00:46:13,041
Even Korean dramas couldn't compete.

817
00:46:13,375 --> 00:46:14,375
It's a new concept.

818
00:46:15,750 --> 00:46:17,250
Now, I'm laughing about it.

819
00:46:17,375 --> 00:46:19,125
Back then, it hurt me a lot.

820
00:46:20,750 --> 00:46:23,125
How did you manage
to fall in love again?

821
00:46:23,291 --> 00:46:26,208
Sir, do you know what the medicine
for love failure is?

822
00:46:26,458 --> 00:46:27,666
Is there a medicine for it?

823
00:46:27,916 --> 00:46:29,166
It's falling in love again.

824
00:46:30,541 --> 00:46:32,250
We moved to Chennai for our college.

825
00:46:32,750 --> 00:46:34,000
My uncle moved with us.

826
00:46:35,208 --> 00:46:37,875
<i>The days when we graduated
from college and had no jobs.</i>

827
00:46:38,000 --> 00:46:42,415
We're coming for a live telecast
on Thanga Uncle's terrace

828
00:46:42,416 --> 00:46:44,665
to watch the Cricket World Cup final.

829
00:46:44,666 --> 00:46:46,582
Dearest Sachin Tendulkar.

830
00:46:46,583 --> 00:46:48,750
Sweetheart Sehwag.
They're entering the pitch.

831
00:46:48,916 --> 00:46:50,666
Hey, I'm going to whack you.

832
00:46:50,875 --> 00:46:55,665
Priest, wait and watch, in the future,
Tamil commentary is going to be worse.

833
00:46:55,666 --> 00:46:56,957
And you'll be laughing at it.

834
00:46:56,958 --> 00:47:01,125
Hey, if they had employed our people,
they would've rocked it.

835
00:47:01,583 --> 00:47:03,208
Isn't cricket already
under your people's control?

836
00:47:03,416 --> 00:47:04,583
Please calm down.

837
00:47:08,083 --> 00:47:09,958
Uncle, you're something else, I say.

838
00:47:10,208 --> 00:47:12,457
You're telecasting the match on the
terrace and making tea in the kitchen.

839
00:47:12,458 --> 00:47:13,833
I wanted to watch the
match at the stadium.

840
00:47:14,000 --> 00:47:14,957
I couldn't get tickets.

841
00:47:14,958 --> 00:47:17,332
Also, I had saved some money
to watch the match.

842
00:47:17,333 --> 00:47:19,208
Since I couldn't make it to the stadium,

843
00:47:19,416 --> 00:47:21,290
I wanted to bring
the stadium atmosphere right here.

844
00:47:21,291 --> 00:47:22,790
So, I installed a screen upstairs.

845
00:47:22,791 --> 00:47:24,583
Venu, sentiment, is it?

846
00:47:25,416 --> 00:47:26,582
What sentiment?

847
00:47:26,583 --> 00:47:28,415
During the 1983 World Cup,

848
00:47:28,416 --> 00:47:30,249
Nallapadiandavar
stood with one leg just like this.

849
00:47:30,250 --> 00:47:31,583
He's following the same sentiment.

850
00:47:31,750 --> 00:47:33,290
Mr. Venu, don't put your leg down.

851
00:47:33,291 --> 00:47:35,332
If India wins the World Cup today…

852
00:47:35,333 --> 00:47:37,540
I'm going to order three big pots
of briyani from Charminar Briyani

853
00:47:37,541 --> 00:47:38,624
and give it as food donation.

854
00:47:38,625 --> 00:47:40,582
You'll be the first one to give
briyani as donation.

855
00:47:40,583 --> 00:47:42,375
- Are you serious?
- Yes!

856
00:47:42,916 --> 00:47:44,041
What's happening upstairs?

857
00:47:44,708 --> 00:47:47,500
You have installed a screen and
are telecasting the match like a movie.

858
00:47:48,166 --> 00:47:51,250
Don't you know you must inform
the Ward Councilor about it?

859
00:47:51,625 --> 00:47:54,124
After the 83's, only now
we're getting to see the World Cup.

860
00:47:54,125 --> 00:47:57,125
Even the Prime Minister is waiting
at the stadium to see them win.

861
00:47:57,250 --> 00:47:59,915
And you're here whining about the
clerk and the counselor. Oh, God!

862
00:47:59,916 --> 00:48:01,790
Even now, you won't invite me
to the match, right?

863
00:48:01,791 --> 00:48:03,499
Please come and watch.
Who's stopping you?

864
00:48:03,500 --> 00:48:05,707
The match is for everyone.
Please come and watch.

865
00:48:05,708 --> 00:48:06,707
Serve it to everyone.

866
00:48:06,708 --> 00:48:08,750
Hey, Uncle is here with the tea.
We can expect a sixer.

867
00:48:09,416 --> 00:48:10,332
Hey, move aside.

868
00:48:10,333 --> 00:48:12,833
Here comes Ghambir,
bowlers are going to tremble now.

869
00:48:13,333 --> 00:48:15,165
That's a fantastic straight drive.

870
00:48:15,166 --> 00:48:17,583
- Go and serve tea to everyone.
- First, you take a cup.

871
00:48:19,666 --> 00:48:21,375
Dear, are you seriously in love with him?

872
00:48:21,583 --> 00:48:23,500
Uncle, she might say no.
Please go and serve tea.

873
00:48:23,916 --> 00:48:24,833
A lot!

874
00:48:25,625 --> 00:48:27,375
Now this is what you call a match!

875
00:48:27,958 --> 00:48:30,457
- Here, have it.
<i>- You must not have beer on the roof top.</i>

876
00:48:30,458 --> 00:48:33,082
<i>The boss can't digest milk.</i>

877
00:48:33,083 --> 00:48:34,915
Do you have a pickle?
Pickle?

878
00:48:34,916 --> 00:48:37,583
Uncle, those goons are having booze.

879
00:48:37,875 --> 00:48:40,041
And they're asking for a pickle
to have with beer.

880
00:48:40,250 --> 00:48:43,749
It's wrong to have liquor
when women and children are around.

881
00:48:43,750 --> 00:48:45,875
And on top of it, you've asked
for pickles. Leave from here.

882
00:48:46,250 --> 00:48:47,915
How dare you remove us from here?

883
00:48:47,916 --> 00:48:49,750
- I ought to!
- How dare you lay your hands on us?

884
00:48:50,666 --> 00:48:51,875
Hey! Uncle! Uncle!

885
00:48:52,208 --> 00:48:55,332
Brother, why are you getting angry?
Watch the match!

886
00:48:55,333 --> 00:48:56,749
Hand me the bottle,
I'll put it in the fridge.

887
00:48:56,750 --> 00:48:58,708
Once India wins,
we'll have drinks together.

888
00:48:58,916 --> 00:48:59,916
You think India is going to win?

889
00:49:00,708 --> 00:49:01,666
My foot!

890
00:49:02,666 --> 00:49:04,333
<i>Hey, Sachin is out!</i>

891
00:49:04,875 --> 00:49:07,375
Gone! And they're expecting a win!

892
00:49:09,125 --> 00:49:11,125
As long as Dhoni is there,
the match won't end. Wait and watch.

893
00:49:11,250 --> 00:49:12,166
Dhoni…

894
00:49:13,500 --> 00:49:15,416
Brother, you can talk about us
all you want.

895
00:49:15,750 --> 00:49:17,040
But don't speak ill of Dhoni.

896
00:49:17,041 --> 00:49:19,083
Why? Is Dhoni a great player?

897
00:49:27,583 --> 00:49:30,958
<i>There go 4 runs!
And that's a fantastic shot.</i>

898
00:49:33,375 --> 00:49:37,249
<i>Left-hand batsmen hit
is flying towards the trophy.</i>

899
00:49:37,250 --> 00:49:39,083
<i>The fans are stunned by this shot.</i>

900
00:49:42,041 --> 00:49:44,166
<i>Is it going to Sri Lanka or India?</i>

901
00:49:44,291 --> 00:49:46,916
Bring it on!
Come on, come on!

902
00:49:47,125 --> 00:49:50,916
<i>Once again, Gautham Ghambir
delivered a fantastic shot.</i>

903
00:49:51,250 --> 00:49:52,874
<i>That was a fantastic shot.</i>

904
00:49:52,875 --> 00:49:54,957
<i>The ball hit the boundary,
and auntie here is yelling.</i>

905
00:49:54,958 --> 00:49:57,832
Hey, don't block the projector.
That's great, guys!

906
00:49:57,833 --> 00:49:58,749
Is this okay?

907
00:49:58,750 --> 00:50:01,583
<i>He got a gap
and has been scoring 4s continuously.</i>

908
00:50:01,708 --> 00:50:03,458
<i>Amazing game, I say.</i>

909
00:50:03,791 --> 00:50:09,958
<i>Virat Kohli is proving he's also in
this game by scoring boundaries.</i>

910
00:50:10,375 --> 00:50:14,333
<i>Kohli's wicket was caught
like a goalie by Wilson.</i>

911
00:50:19,666 --> 00:50:23,625
<i>The champion batsman Yuvaraj Singh, of
this World Cup series, is coming to bat.</i>

912
00:50:24,083 --> 00:50:25,666
<i>That's a plot twist!</i>

913
00:50:40,791 --> 00:50:42,208
Idhaya, what happened?

914
00:50:42,333 --> 00:50:43,374
First, remove his shirt.

915
00:50:43,375 --> 00:50:45,374
- My eyes are burning.
- What happened?

916
00:50:45,375 --> 00:50:47,165
Bring out the vehicle.
We must take him to the hospital.

917
00:50:47,166 --> 00:50:48,833
- Hey, open your eyes.
- Idhaya! Idhaya!

918
00:50:50,625 --> 00:50:51,625
Buddy, watch out!

919
00:50:53,750 --> 00:50:55,375
Please have him sit carefully.

920
00:50:56,458 --> 00:50:57,625
Fire struck his eye, Doctor.

921
00:50:57,791 --> 00:50:59,583
Please check.
He's not able to open his eyes.

922
00:51:01,250 --> 00:51:02,750
Sir, please open your eyes slowly.

923
00:51:06,916 --> 00:51:08,291
I'm putting some drops.

924
00:51:08,416 --> 00:51:09,791
- He should be fine.
- Dude, is it burning?

925
00:51:11,041 --> 00:51:11,958
Of course!

926
00:51:13,458 --> 00:51:15,666
- Hey, check what the score is?
- Yeah, score!

927
00:51:17,250 --> 00:51:18,500
Look at him, Doctor.

928
00:51:18,666 --> 00:51:20,750
He's more concerned
about the match than his eyes.

929
00:51:20,875 --> 00:51:22,625
Hey, please calm down, dude.

930
00:51:22,833 --> 00:51:24,208
Hey, it's 224/4.

931
00:51:24,958 --> 00:51:26,582
- Where is Uncle?
- I don't know.

932
00:51:26,583 --> 00:51:27,500
Uncle!

933
00:51:50,250 --> 00:51:52,625
<i>And the score is 277/4!</i>

934
00:51:55,208 --> 00:51:58,041
<i>Everyone witnessed
Dhoni's winning shot on TV.</i>

935
00:51:58,458 --> 00:52:00,875
<i>But I witnessed it in her eyes.</i>

936
00:52:06,291 --> 00:52:08,375
Please follow these drops for two days.

937
00:52:09,125 --> 00:52:11,791
Don't make a wrong prescription
while celebrating India's victory.

938
00:52:12,958 --> 00:52:15,082
Hey, Ammu, India won!

939
00:52:15,083 --> 00:52:16,540
Dhoni scored a fantastic sixer
in the last ball.

940
00:52:16,541 --> 00:52:17,500
Why haven't you left yet?

941
00:52:19,875 --> 00:52:20,791
Sachin Bro!

942
00:52:21,666 --> 00:52:24,415
<i>I am ashamed
to call you guys my juniors.</i>

943
00:52:24,416 --> 00:52:25,374
<i>Damn!</i>

944
00:52:25,375 --> 00:52:28,208
- You became a doctor?
- What are you guys doing out here?

945
00:52:28,500 --> 00:52:29,750
This is what happened.

946
00:52:30,208 --> 00:52:32,708
When will you guys change?
Still starting fights everywhere.

947
00:52:33,041 --> 00:52:35,499
Brother, forget about it.
Why are you wearing a coat?

948
00:52:35,500 --> 00:52:37,249
- I'm a doctor.
- Doctor?

949
00:52:37,250 --> 00:52:39,750
Didn't you say kissing leads to pregnancy?
How did you become a doctor?

950
00:52:39,875 --> 00:52:40,958
It's not believable.

951
00:52:41,208 --> 00:52:42,833
Believe me. I'm a Doctor.

952
00:52:43,375 --> 00:52:45,582
Are you serious?
A doctor in our family.

953
00:52:45,583 --> 00:52:47,000
- I feel proud.
- Hey, take your hands off me.

954
00:52:47,708 --> 00:52:51,915
In fact, doctors are truly great.
They make a lot of sacrifices.

955
00:52:51,916 --> 00:52:53,541
- Yes, we work around the clock.
- Wow!

956
00:52:54,000 --> 00:52:56,791
- But as a doctor, everything--
- Hold it right there.

957
00:52:57,208 --> 00:52:58,290
You aren't so nice.

958
00:52:58,291 --> 00:53:00,207
- Why are you praising doctors now?
- Brother, you don't get me.

959
00:53:00,208 --> 00:53:01,541
- Sachin!
- It's a great profession--

960
00:53:02,041 --> 00:53:03,875
What are you doing?
It's getting late. Let's go.

961
00:53:04,458 --> 00:53:05,915
- Who is that, bro?
- My girlfriend.

962
00:53:05,916 --> 00:53:07,750
- Your girlfriend?
- Yeah!

963
00:53:07,875 --> 00:53:08,957
Stop lying to us.

964
00:53:08,958 --> 00:53:12,416
Hey, guys,
these people are my school juniors.

965
00:53:12,791 --> 00:53:14,665
- Hi!
- This is Lado, and this is Ammu.

966
00:53:14,666 --> 00:53:15,791
- Hi.
- And they're my college juniors.

967
00:53:16,708 --> 00:53:17,749
Hi!

968
00:53:17,750 --> 00:53:20,499
They don't believe me
that you're my girlfriend.

969
00:53:20,500 --> 00:53:22,125
- Is it?
- Yes!

970
00:53:22,500 --> 00:53:25,874
When you say a beautiful girl like me
is dating a guy like him,

971
00:53:25,875 --> 00:53:28,165
- people may find it hard to believe.
- Hey, that's enough!

972
00:53:28,166 --> 00:53:29,708
I was just kidding. Relax!

973
00:53:30,666 --> 00:53:32,166
Is your eye okay now?

974
00:53:32,708 --> 00:53:33,625
Much better!

975
00:53:34,333 --> 00:53:36,875
If the pain persists,
please come back tomorrow.

976
00:53:37,625 --> 00:53:38,541
Okay.

977
00:53:39,416 --> 00:53:41,041
I'm here to meet the girl I like.

978
00:53:42,250 --> 00:53:44,166
- My eyes are cured now.
- Yes!

979
00:53:46,583 --> 00:53:48,999
It won't be nice
if I don't bring her anything.

980
00:53:49,000 --> 00:53:52,833
Why don't you buy a rose
and a greeting card for her?

981
00:53:54,416 --> 00:53:56,500
- He's right!
- Hey! Get out of here!

982
00:53:56,916 --> 00:53:58,124
He's giving lame old ideas.

983
00:53:58,125 --> 00:53:59,665
- We'll do something new.
- Hey, the rose might--

984
00:53:59,666 --> 00:54:01,999
Rose, greeting card,
and gifting a pair of pigeons…

985
00:54:02,000 --> 00:54:04,083
It's all an old concept and is outdated.

986
00:54:04,291 --> 00:54:05,375
You must think fresh and trendy.

987
00:54:05,625 --> 00:54:06,707
I doubt following the trend…

988
00:54:06,708 --> 00:54:07,832
Brother, please help me out.

989
00:54:07,833 --> 00:54:10,083
She's in labor.
Please help me with her.

990
00:54:10,208 --> 00:54:12,250
- Don't think. It's an emergency.
- Why us?

991
00:54:12,416 --> 00:54:14,833
- Hey, let's check it out.
- Madam, bear a little, we're almost there.

992
00:54:15,625 --> 00:54:17,874
- Ma'am, watch your step.
- Someone, please help!

993
00:54:17,875 --> 00:54:19,749
Brother, bring out the gurney.

994
00:54:19,750 --> 00:54:21,333
Instead of waiting, you could carry her.

995
00:54:21,500 --> 00:54:23,458
- Please carry her.
- Hey, carry her!

996
00:54:25,125 --> 00:54:26,082
Don't be scared.

997
00:54:26,083 --> 00:54:27,875
- Watch out.
- Carry her.

998
00:54:28,125 --> 00:54:29,625
- Come on, carry her.
- This way.

999
00:54:29,750 --> 00:54:31,333
- Watch your step.
- Please be careful.

1000
00:54:33,041 --> 00:54:34,375
Brother, come along.

1001
00:54:34,750 --> 00:54:37,875
Brother, it's not always necessary
for an auto driver to help during labor.

1002
00:54:38,083 --> 00:54:40,124
- You too can help her.
- Get lost!

1003
00:54:40,125 --> 00:54:41,999
Dude, you thought
you didn't get her anything.

1004
00:54:42,000 --> 00:54:43,500
But God has graced you with a huge gift.

1005
00:54:44,041 --> 00:54:45,832
Hey, ask which way the labor ward is.

1006
00:54:45,833 --> 00:54:47,416
- Doctor! Over here.
- Careful.

1007
00:54:47,541 --> 00:54:49,416
- She's in labor pain. Check on her.
- It's an emergency.

1008
00:54:50,708 --> 00:54:51,958
Her pulse is high.

1009
00:54:52,375 --> 00:54:53,790
- Where's the gurney?
- No need for that.

1010
00:54:53,791 --> 00:54:55,458
Bring her over to that room.

1011
00:54:56,750 --> 00:54:58,416
Careful! Careful! Slowly.

1012
00:55:01,458 --> 00:55:04,374
- Nurse, quickly check her blood pressure.
- Yes, Doctor.

1013
00:55:04,375 --> 00:55:05,666
Don't worry. You'll be fine.

1014
00:55:05,875 --> 00:55:08,165
- Nurse, prep for the procedure.
- You're okay. Doing great!

1015
00:55:08,166 --> 00:55:10,499
- Let's go.
- Check if we have all the medicines.

1016
00:55:10,500 --> 00:55:12,333
- Why are you still standing over there?
- Sir?

1017
00:55:13,291 --> 00:55:16,749
How long are men going to keep avoiding
being by their wives' side during labor?

1018
00:55:16,750 --> 00:55:19,083
Go and witness the struggle
she's going through.

1019
00:55:19,250 --> 00:55:21,915
- Oh, no, you have got it wrong.
- It's wrong. Come with me.

1020
00:55:21,916 --> 00:55:23,624
- Nurse, I'm not her husband--
- Come on!

1021
00:55:23,625 --> 00:55:24,875
- Please hear me out.
- Go inside!

1022
00:55:26,500 --> 00:55:28,083
Turn around. Wear this.

1023
00:55:28,500 --> 00:55:29,999
Is this your first pregnancy?

1024
00:55:30,000 --> 00:55:33,083
Previous pregnancy, C-section,
or any complications?

1025
00:55:33,250 --> 00:55:35,250
What's her blood group? A, B, O?

1026
00:55:35,916 --> 00:55:38,375
- Any allergies?
- Yeah, she sneezed on her way here.

1027
00:55:39,625 --> 00:55:42,083
- When did she go into labor?
- The vehicle just arrived.

1028
00:55:42,291 --> 00:55:44,125
- I'm asking about labor pains.
- Don't worry. You'll be fine.

1029
00:55:44,875 --> 00:55:45,791
Bend down.

1030
00:55:46,458 --> 00:55:48,000
He does not know anything!

1031
00:55:48,500 --> 00:55:51,083
- Hurry up! I can't bear the pain.
- It's okay.

1032
00:55:51,666 --> 00:55:54,166
- Nurse, quickly prep the delivery tray.
- It's ready.

1033
00:55:54,416 --> 00:55:56,625
Bloody man,
how could you not know anything?

1034
00:55:56,791 --> 00:55:58,707
This pregnant lady's
curse won't spare you.

1035
00:55:58,708 --> 00:56:00,166
Go and give her some courage.

1036
00:56:00,750 --> 00:56:01,875
Go ahead, man!

1037
00:56:02,000 --> 00:56:03,958
Hello! Please be brave.

1038
00:56:04,125 --> 00:56:06,165
- Please be brave.
- Hold his hand.

1039
00:56:06,166 --> 00:56:07,125
Hold it tight!

1040
00:56:08,166 --> 00:56:09,916
- Please be brave.
- I'm on my way, Doctor.

1041
00:56:10,166 --> 00:56:12,666
- Be brave.
- Push, push. You can do it.

1042
00:56:12,791 --> 00:56:13,707
Take a deep breath.

1043
00:56:13,708 --> 00:56:15,915
- Doctor, she's fully dilated.
- Okay.

1044
00:56:15,916 --> 00:56:17,708
- Push! Push!
- You can do it!

1045
00:56:17,833 --> 00:56:19,707
Come on. Come on.
One more push.

1046
00:56:19,708 --> 00:56:21,541
Why do you have your back
turned to your wife?

1047
00:56:31,458 --> 00:56:33,416
- Something is not right.
- You're right!

1048
00:56:33,958 --> 00:56:35,665
A woman comes in an auto in labor.

1049
00:56:35,666 --> 00:56:37,375
And he'll carry her to the ward.

1050
00:56:37,708 --> 00:56:39,915
And he stays back during the labor.

1051
00:56:39,916 --> 00:56:40,833
I can't believe it.

1052
00:56:41,208 --> 00:56:43,583
- Very wrong!
- He's always been this person.

1053
00:56:43,708 --> 00:56:45,583
Right! When he was 10,
he signed for his teacher.

1054
00:56:46,125 --> 00:56:49,749
Hey, why didn't you tell them
you're not her husband?

1055
00:56:49,750 --> 00:56:51,250
They never let me speak.

1056
00:56:51,541 --> 00:56:53,041
Moreover, her husband wasn't with her.

1057
00:56:54,041 --> 00:56:55,666
I felt very bad for her.

1058
00:56:59,000 --> 00:57:01,000
Mom would've struggled
the same way, right?

1059
00:57:01,125 --> 00:57:03,041
Hey, it's a comedy scene.

1060
00:57:03,375 --> 00:57:04,708
Don't turn it into
a mother-sentiment scene.

1061
00:57:05,625 --> 00:57:06,958
Do you think
Amudha would've misunderstood me?

1062
00:57:07,708 --> 00:57:09,791
Sounds like Idhaya likes her a lot.

1063
00:57:10,916 --> 00:57:12,250
Nothing like that.

1064
00:57:13,041 --> 00:57:15,249
I couldn't get you married
to the girl you like.

1065
00:57:15,250 --> 00:57:17,458
But do you think
I wouldn't know who you like?

1066
00:57:22,208 --> 00:57:23,958
Why is she calling me now?
Hello?

1067
00:57:25,500 --> 00:57:26,416
Oh, no!

1068
00:57:27,416 --> 00:57:29,541
What are you saying? Where?

1069
00:57:31,333 --> 00:57:32,333
I'll be right there!

1070
00:57:34,875 --> 00:57:35,791
What happened?

1071
00:57:37,916 --> 00:57:40,666
- What happened?
- Lado and Amudha have no other business.

1072
00:57:40,875 --> 00:57:43,500
They got caught by the traffic police.
Ignore it!

1073
00:57:44,916 --> 00:57:46,541
What are you saying?
Let's help them.

1074
00:57:46,791 --> 00:57:50,208
Basically, when girls get caught and cry,
they let them go.

1075
00:57:50,708 --> 00:57:53,291
But our women are arrogant to the max.

1076
00:57:53,541 --> 00:57:55,791
They would've run their mouth.
And got caught.

1077
00:57:55,916 --> 00:57:57,041
Bro, Amudha is out there.

1078
00:57:57,583 --> 00:57:58,916
Uncle, make him understand.

1079
00:57:59,291 --> 00:58:01,540
Yes, you guys carry on.
I'll take care of the booze.

1080
00:58:01,541 --> 00:58:03,875
- I'll take care of Uncle.
- Didn't you say we must help others?

1081
00:58:04,000 --> 00:58:05,750
Now what? Only if you
come along will others follow.

1082
00:58:05,875 --> 00:58:06,791
Please, come with me.

1083
00:58:07,166 --> 00:58:10,040
- He's a nuisance.
- Sachin, even the police would spare them.

1084
00:58:10,041 --> 00:58:11,500
But he won't spare us.
Let's get them.

1085
00:58:11,916 --> 00:58:13,875
- Hey, Idhaya, let's go after this drink.
- Let's go!

1086
00:58:14,500 --> 00:58:17,665
Lately, women get drunk
and cause a ruckus.

1087
00:58:17,666 --> 00:58:19,083
- Yes, sir.
- Hey, Policeman!

1088
00:58:19,291 --> 00:58:21,582
Do you think drinking alcohol
is only men's right?

1089
00:58:21,583 --> 00:58:23,208
- Stop talking nonsense!
- Please shut up.

1090
00:58:28,500 --> 00:58:30,165
- No one gets out of the car.
- Okay, dude.

1091
00:58:30,166 --> 00:58:31,291
Everyone, wait here.

1092
00:58:32,333 --> 00:58:33,750
Please stop talking.

1093
00:58:33,958 --> 00:58:35,541
How could he speak so disrespectfully?

1094
00:58:35,666 --> 00:58:37,207
How dare he say whatever he wants?

1095
00:58:37,208 --> 00:58:39,374
Hello, how dare you call me a dog!

1096
00:58:39,375 --> 00:58:42,333
I won't insult the dogs
by comparing them to you.

1097
00:58:43,708 --> 00:58:45,249
- Lado, please--
- What happened?

1098
00:58:45,250 --> 00:58:46,790
Look, he's going overboard.

1099
00:58:46,791 --> 00:58:48,791
- Please calm down for a minute.
- Where's Sachin? Call him.

1100
00:58:49,041 --> 00:58:50,291
Lado, please calm down for a moment.

1101
00:58:50,750 --> 00:58:51,666
What happened?

1102
00:58:51,791 --> 00:58:53,332
I was driving the car.

1103
00:58:53,333 --> 00:58:56,416
They checked and asked me to go.
But she spoke out of turn.

1104
00:58:56,791 --> 00:58:59,665
This police officer
looks like trouble to me.

1105
00:58:59,666 --> 00:59:02,082
- Yes!
- Oh, she's a doctor, is she?

1106
00:59:02,083 --> 00:59:04,250
That doesn't give her the right
to speak down to the police.

1107
00:59:04,375 --> 00:59:05,375
How could she call me a dog?

1108
00:59:05,583 --> 00:59:07,708
- Sir, please forgive them.
- Why should I listen to you?

1109
00:59:07,833 --> 00:59:10,875
- Get to the side.
- Sir, I know my rules.

1110
00:59:11,208 --> 00:59:12,500
Only the co-passenger was drunk.

1111
00:59:12,791 --> 00:59:14,666
The driver wasn't drunk.
Why are you holding them?

1112
00:59:14,791 --> 00:59:16,708
Talking rules, is it? Super!

1113
00:59:17,000 --> 00:59:18,332
- Sir, please understand…
- Sir! Sir!

1114
00:59:18,333 --> 00:59:20,000
- Sir!
- What's the issue?

1115
00:59:20,166 --> 00:59:22,166
Sir, it's a DD case.
I'm investigating, sir.

1116
00:59:23,125 --> 00:59:25,999
Sir, only the co-passenger was drunk.
The driver wasn't drunk.

1117
00:59:26,000 --> 00:59:27,458
They're causing unnecessary problems.

1118
00:59:27,583 --> 00:59:30,333
Sir, he's distracting you.
Don't believe him.

1119
00:59:30,625 --> 00:59:32,541
Hey, stay normal.

1120
00:59:32,833 --> 00:59:33,750
Sir.

1121
00:59:34,500 --> 00:59:36,208
You've become a nuisance lately.

1122
00:59:37,208 --> 00:59:38,750
- Send them away.
- Thank you, sir.

1123
00:59:41,500 --> 00:59:42,416
Get in, let's go.

1124
00:59:43,333 --> 00:59:44,750
Lado, get inside the car.

1125
00:59:45,666 --> 00:59:47,290
Super! Idhaya solved the issue.

1126
00:59:47,291 --> 00:59:51,375
Hey, did you see my nephew?
He smartly handled the situation.

1127
00:59:51,500 --> 00:59:53,791
Smart, my foot!
Who's going to drive us home?

1128
00:59:54,583 --> 00:59:57,040
- Yes! Who's going to drive us?
- Is my mouth stinking?

1129
00:59:57,041 --> 00:59:58,708
- It's not stinking.
- Not at all, Uncle.

1130
00:59:58,833 --> 01:00:01,333
Now we've become friends of the police.
I'll drive.

1131
01:00:02,541 --> 01:00:04,625
Come on, drive, Uncle.

1132
01:00:05,166 --> 01:00:07,500
Uncle, we should arrive home
before they do.

1133
01:00:07,833 --> 01:00:09,000
Watch me drive now!

1134
01:00:13,166 --> 01:00:14,665
- Hey, ask them to leave.
- Leave!

1135
01:00:14,666 --> 01:00:16,333
- Leave!
- Drive, Uncle.

1136
01:00:16,458 --> 01:00:20,165
- Don't you know who we are?
- Uncle, why are you bringing it up?

1137
01:00:20,166 --> 01:00:22,415
- The gang that went before us…
- Yes!

1138
01:00:22,416 --> 01:00:23,458
…we're part of the same gang.

1139
01:00:24,416 --> 01:00:26,208
- He's a doctor.
- His tattoo says it too.

1140
01:00:26,916 --> 01:00:28,666
There's a sticker that says so, too.

1141
01:00:28,833 --> 01:00:29,791
Sir, there's a sticker.

1142
01:00:29,958 --> 01:00:31,458
A sticker doesn't prove
that you're a doctor.

1143
01:00:31,875 --> 01:00:34,291
Why is everyone
announcing themselves as doctors?

1144
01:00:34,416 --> 01:00:36,040
How dare you
sit inside the car disrespectfully?

1145
01:00:36,041 --> 01:00:36,957
Step out of the car.

1146
01:00:36,958 --> 01:00:39,207
Why would you get us into trouble, uncle?
Step out!

1147
01:00:39,208 --> 01:00:40,625
Step out of the car.

1148
01:00:50,083 --> 01:00:51,625
- Is he a doctor?
- Exactly, sir.

1149
01:00:51,791 --> 01:00:53,375
I think he doesn't believe you.

1150
01:00:54,041 --> 01:00:55,583
Say a few medicine names aloud.

1151
01:00:57,708 --> 01:01:01,916
Anacin, Crocin, Dolo
650, and Azithromycin.

1152
01:01:03,333 --> 01:01:04,749
See, he's a doctor.

1153
01:01:04,750 --> 01:01:09,832
Vicks Action 500, Paracetamol,
Vicks, Halls, Strepsils.

1154
01:01:09,833 --> 01:01:11,249
- Are you a doctor too?
- Halls?

1155
01:01:11,250 --> 01:01:13,041
Then how did you end up
in the police department?

1156
01:01:13,166 --> 01:01:15,665
Hey! Even a grocery store owner
can list these medicines.

1157
01:01:15,666 --> 01:01:18,124
Naming these medicines won't prove
you're a doctor. Get inside the car.

1158
01:01:18,125 --> 01:01:20,500
- Come on, let's go!
- Hey, where are you going?

1159
01:01:20,625 --> 01:01:21,540
Get inside this car.

1160
01:01:21,541 --> 01:01:22,790
- This one?
- Get inside this vehicle.

1161
01:01:22,791 --> 01:01:24,208
- Come on, get inside.
- Oh, no…

1162
01:01:24,791 --> 01:01:25,708
Come in!

1163
01:01:28,375 --> 01:01:30,291
Welcome home!

1164
01:01:31,541 --> 01:01:33,875
- Would you like to have something?
- What's this mess?

1165
01:01:34,083 --> 01:01:36,291
We got caught by the police

1166
01:01:36,458 --> 01:01:39,291
but you guys here were
chilling and boozing.

1167
01:01:40,250 --> 01:01:41,333
- Hey, calm down.
<i>- Dude.</i>

1168
01:01:41,625 --> 01:01:43,332
- Dude, we got caught by the police.
- Hey, Lado!

1169
01:01:43,333 --> 01:01:45,000
- Can you hear me?
<i>- Hello! Hello!</i>

1170
01:01:45,125 --> 01:01:46,457
<i>- Can you hear me?</i>
- Yes, I can. Tell me.

1171
01:01:46,458 --> 01:01:48,250
Who's it? Is it Sachin?

1172
01:01:48,625 --> 01:01:50,540
Give it to me.
Hello! What happened?

1173
01:01:50,541 --> 01:01:53,374
We trusted Uncle to drive
and got caught by the police.

1174
01:01:53,375 --> 01:01:55,875
- Who's speaking?
- Aww, so sad!

1175
01:01:56,250 --> 01:01:57,250
- So sad!
<i>- Yes, baby!</i>

1176
01:01:57,416 --> 01:01:58,583
You'd better rot out there.

1177
01:01:58,708 --> 01:02:00,333
What did you tell me
when I called you for help?

1178
01:02:00,458 --> 01:02:03,291
- Hey, hey, babe!
- Don't say anything.

1179
01:02:03,833 --> 01:02:05,624
- Don't you call yourself a boyfriend.
- Dad's calling.

1180
01:02:05,625 --> 01:02:06,707
Your dad?

1181
01:02:06,708 --> 01:02:09,375
- Go to the roof top and talk.
- I noticed empty bottles here.

1182
01:02:09,625 --> 01:02:12,291
- Baby, please send someone to help.
- Who are you talking to?

1183
01:02:13,750 --> 01:02:14,666
Give me the phone.

1184
01:02:15,833 --> 01:02:17,875
<i>- Be careful, dear.</i>
- Okay, Dad.

1185
01:02:18,708 --> 01:02:20,249
<i>Please eat on time and sleep.</i>

1186
01:02:20,250 --> 01:02:21,208
Please go to sleep.

1187
01:02:21,375 --> 01:02:22,291
<i>Sure, dear!</i>

1188
01:02:22,666 --> 01:02:23,832
I'm going to sleep now.

1189
01:02:23,833 --> 01:02:25,375
- Lado?
- She slept.

1190
01:02:25,750 --> 01:02:27,916
<i>- Take care.</i>
- I'll call you in the morning.

1191
01:02:28,083 --> 01:02:30,458
<i>- Okay, dear.</i>
- Okay, bye, Dad.

1192
01:02:34,208 --> 01:02:35,125
It was Dad.

1193
01:02:35,625 --> 01:02:38,833
Asking about my
whereabouts and activities.

1194
01:02:39,375 --> 01:02:42,666
He takes care of me like I'm a child.

1195
01:02:45,958 --> 01:02:47,041
How about your family?

1196
01:02:47,750 --> 01:02:49,375
No issues in my family.

1197
01:02:49,666 --> 01:02:51,958
It's always fun for sons.

1198
01:02:52,291 --> 01:02:53,250
That's not the case.

1199
01:02:54,000 --> 01:02:55,583
I don't have parents.

1200
01:02:57,750 --> 01:02:58,750
I'm sorry, Idhaya.

1201
01:02:59,333 --> 01:03:01,291
It's okay. I have my Uncle.

1202
01:03:02,500 --> 01:03:04,791
He's equal to a hundred parents.
He's great at it!

1203
01:03:10,791 --> 01:03:12,666
What's this DTV?

1204
01:03:14,416 --> 01:03:15,875
Oh, this?

1205
01:03:16,166 --> 01:03:17,666
It's our local cable TV channel.

1206
01:03:17,833 --> 01:03:20,250
My Uncle and I dream of
making that into a satellite channel.

1207
01:03:20,500 --> 01:03:22,458
- Super!
- Thanks!

1208
01:03:27,750 --> 01:03:28,875
Would you like to have something?

1209
01:03:29,791 --> 01:03:30,708
No!

1210
01:03:31,916 --> 01:03:33,458
Can I get a simple cup of tea?

1211
01:03:34,000 --> 01:03:36,750
Not sure about a simple cup of tea, but
I can get you the best tea in the world.

1212
01:03:37,250 --> 01:03:38,250
Would you adjust?

1213
01:03:39,791 --> 01:03:41,791
- Okay.
- I'll bring it.

1214
01:03:52,583 --> 01:03:53,500
How's it?

1215
01:03:55,958 --> 01:03:58,791
What's the special ingredient
of the world's best tea?

1216
01:04:00,000 --> 01:04:01,500
<i>Add tea powder to boiling water.</i>

1217
01:04:01,625 --> 01:04:04,833
<i>Then add a piece of ginger
and sprinkle Tulasi over it.</i>

1218
01:04:05,041 --> 01:04:07,583
<i>Finally, add lots of love…</i>

1219
01:04:07,875 --> 01:04:10,083
If you have this tea, you won't forget
its taste for the rest of your life.

1220
01:04:13,083 --> 01:04:15,166
You added a lot of ingredients,
but did you add sugar?

1221
01:04:16,375 --> 01:04:17,291
Sugar?

1222
01:04:22,958 --> 01:04:24,666
Shall I add sugar and bring it back?

1223
01:04:25,541 --> 01:04:27,250
It's okay.
I'm liking this taste.

1224
01:04:28,583 --> 01:04:29,500
Sorry.

1225
01:04:34,291 --> 01:04:37,791
From now on, every cup of tea
will remind me of this one.

1226
01:04:38,083 --> 01:04:39,916
- You mean this sugarless tea?
- Yes!

1227
01:05:11,750 --> 01:05:15,583
<i>With dreams in tow,
I came to tell a story</i>

1228
01:05:15,750 --> 01:05:19,416
<i>With memories lingering,
I stood in a different hue</i>

1229
01:05:19,666 --> 01:05:23,291
<i>Through you,
I saw miracles beyond reality</i>

1230
01:05:23,500 --> 01:05:26,958
<i>You made me feel happiness
Unknown to me</i>

1231
01:05:27,208 --> 01:05:30,791
<i>The heavens, vast and infinite…</i>

1232
01:05:31,041 --> 01:05:34,375
<i>Won't a tender drizzle grace me?</i>

1233
01:05:34,500 --> 01:05:38,708
<i>And in it…</i>

1234
01:05:38,875 --> 01:05:42,666
<i>My soul yearns to be drenched too</i>

1235
01:05:43,000 --> 01:05:46,833
<i>Where friendship thrives, sorrow fades
The heart carries no weight</i>

1236
01:05:47,166 --> 01:05:50,708
<i>The path unfolds in bloom
When you're by my side</i>

1237
01:05:50,833 --> 01:05:54,666
<i>No path is found unfelt
No love exists unbroken</i>

1238
01:05:54,791 --> 01:05:58,250
<i>No scar is too deep
When it belongs to the tale</i>

1239
01:06:14,166 --> 01:06:17,666
<i>With dreams in tow,
